================================================================================
PURPOSE
================================================================================

Add Growth as a new KNOuX intelligence family — as ADK sub-agents of the existing
root agent, using the existing sub_agents mechanism the file already uses for
google_search_agent and url_context_agent.

NOT a rewrite. The Repair root agent, its instruction, its identity, its safety
policy, its knowledge loader and its MCP wiring are left intact. Growth is
added beside Repair.

Also introduces a model indirection so the reasoning provider can be replaced
without touching agent declarations (defect D8).

================================================================================
D8 — a single model declaration point
================================================================================

PROBLEM
  GlobalGemini(model='gemini-3.5-flash') is repeated in all three agents
  (agent.py:323, 336, 349). Changing the model means editing three call sites,
  which is how they drift.

REPAIR
  One constant, used everywhere.

--- a/agent.py
+++ b/agent.py
@@ after the GlobalGemini class definition
+
+# Single declaration point for the reasoning provider. Everything else refers
+# to this, so changing provider or model is a one-line edit. This is the same
+# indirection KNOuX Growth uses on its own side in
+# src/lib/growth/intelligence/router.ts.
+KNOUX_REASONING_MODEL = "gemini-3.5-flash"
+
+
+def knoux_model() -> Gemini:
+    """Build the agent model.

+    Kept as a factory rather than a module constant because `Gemini` instances
+    hold a client, and sharing one across agents would share session state
+    across independent agents.
+    """
+    return GlobalGemini(model=KNOUX_REASONING_MODEL)

Then, at agent.py:323, 336 and 349:

-  model=GlobalGemini(model='gemini-3.5-flash'),
+  model=knoux_model(),

  To swap providers, change knoux_model() alone.

