================================================================================
SEQUENCING — why Growth cannot land before the MCP bridge
================================================================================

The Growth sub-agents above declare no connector tools, and that is intentional.

Right now the gateway publishes exactly one tool (`gateway_status`), and
tool_filter is set to that one. If these sub-agents were declared with a wider
tool_filter against the current gateway, they would load with an empty tool list
and the model would fall back on general knowledge for anything platform-shaped —
which is precisely the failure this product is built to prevent.

Correct order:

  1. knoux-agent-repair.patch          (the four minimal fixes)
  2. Add MCP tools to the Cloud Run gateway:
       meta.account.list, meta.pages.list, meta.instagram.list,
       meta.ads.accounts, meta.campaigns.list, meta.campaign.read,
       meta.insights.read, meta.leads.read,
       google.ads.accounts, google.ads.campaigns, google.ads.performance,
       google.business.locations, google.business.performance,
       google.analytics.report, google.searchconsole.performance,
       whatsapp.account.status, whatsapp.templates, whatsapp.leads
     Capability definitions for all of these are in
     src/lib/growth/connectors/registry.ts.
  3. Widen tool_filter to that list.
  4. Deploy the agent.
  5. Set KNOUX_AGENT_ENDPOINT and KNOUX_AGENT_TOKEN.
  6. Only then does AGENT_FAMILIES_LIVE change in
     src/lib/growth/intelligence/adapters/knoux-agent.ts, which currently
     deliberately serves REPAIR only.

  MUTATING capabilities (meta.campaign.create, whatsapp.send) must NOT be added
  to the gateway. They are registered as MUTATING and the KNOuX connector
  boundary refuses them outright. Campaign creation runs behind the approval
  gate on the KNOuX side, not through the agent's tool list.

